{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>I believed</b> — Rabbi Moses said: now I will believe that what I was speaking in my heart was truth, as he said, \"Return, my soul.\" And the meaning of עניתי is like דלותי (I was impoverished), from the root עני, and like זמיר עריצים יענה. And the meaning: I said. Regarding the occasion on which it was written, [it was] when it is written [in Samuel], \"And David hastened to go,\" and the meaning of כל האדם כוזב is either that every man lies regarding Samuel who promised him, or כוזב like לא יכזבו, and the meaning is cut off [i.e., he despaired] because he thought he would be killed. And in my opinion: now I will believe when I speak, for formerly I spoke lies, and thus עניתי, like ויען איוב הראשון, and ענית ואמרת."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 116, :notes {0 "The phrase והטעם נכרת is ambiguous; rendered hyper-literally as 'the meaning is cut off,' possibly indicating the psalmist's despair or that the sense is elided. The referent of Rabbi Moses is uncertain; resolved by inference to R. Moses Ibn Ezra (his relative)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:53.668942175Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}